course: dictionary
lesson: 3880
title: Freely: not held back, for free, or willingly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Freely is an adverb, so it tells us how something happens. It has three main meanings: without being stopped or controlled, without having to pay, and openly and willingly. The words around it show you which meaning you need.
explain: «Serfs were farmers who could not leave freely.» The clue is could not leave, so freely means not allowed to go where they wanted. Swap in «could not leave without being stopped» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «A fair swap is one both people agree to freely.» Nobody is forced, so freely means willingly. Watch for «freely available» too: it means you do not have to pay for it.
fact: Freely means without being stopped, held back or controlled.
fact: Freely also means without having to pay, as in «freely available».
fact: Freely can mean openly and willingly, as in «freely admit».
fact: A swap is fair when both people freely agree and nobody uses a threat.
fact: In science, particles can move freely in a gas, and water can flow freely.
exercise: «Serfs could not leave freely.» What does freely mean here? | Happily, with a smile | *Without being stopped or controlled | For no money | Very quickly
exercise: Ella sees a sign: «Museum entry is freely available.» What does freely mean? | *You do not have to pay | You must buy a ticket at the shop | It is only for grown-ups | It is very old
exercise: «Ana freely admitted she had broken the vase.» What does freely suggest? | *She told the truth openly and willingly | She paid for a new vase | She was forced to speak by a teacher | She spoke very quietly
test: «Public broadcasters are meant to report freely.» What does freely mean? | Quietly, in a whisper | Only at night | Badly, with many mistakes | *Without being controlled by the government
test: Which sentence uses freely to mean without paying? | She freely admitted she was wrong | Birds can move freely in the sky | *Museum entry is freely available, so nobody has to pay | Museum entry is freely available, so nobody pays
exam: «A fair swap is one both people agree to freely.» Which meaning of freely fits here? | Very loudly | *Openly and willingly, with no threat | Without being allowed to leave | Without having to pay
